{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FjbCZfkau2ZqbykbZG3qZp","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: rel00.0-uc004-testutils\n     2→title: \"Execute differential tests and compare binary outputs via pkg/testutils\"\n     3→\n     4→summary: |\n     5→  The operator verifies that pkg/testutils correctly executes Go and reference binaries\n     6→  with identical inputs, compares their outputs, and reports divergence. The test exercises\n     7→  each harness capability in isolation: RunDiffTests runs named subtests and compares\n     8→  stdout, stderr, and exit code byte-for-byte; normalization hooks strip non-deterministic\n     9→  fields before comparison; ComposeNormalizers chains multiple hooks; file-state comparison\n    10→  validates output files for utilities like sponge; and the timeout mechanism prevents\n    11→  hanging test runs.\n    12→\n    13→actor: Human Operator\n    14→\n    15→trigger: |\n    16→  The operator has completed the PRD revision (prd001-testutils.yaml) and wants to verify\n    17→  that pkg/testutils satisfies its requirements via unit tests.\n    18→\n    19→flow:\n    20→  - id: F1\n    21→    step: |\n    22→      The operator runs go test ./pkg/testutils/... which executes the unit tests for\n    23→      pkg/testutils. Unlike cmd/ packages that use differential testing against a reference\n    24→      binary, pkg/testutils is the harness itself. Its tests use mock binaries (small shell\n    25→      scripts or compiled test helpers) that produce known stdout, stderr, and exit codes.\n    26→  - id: F2\n    27→    step: |\n    28→      The DiffTest struct test verifies that all fields are accessible and that the zero\n    29→      value produces a valid test case: no args, nil stdin (EOF), nil env (defaults with\n    30→      LC_ALL=C), empty WorkDir (t.TempDir), exit code 0, no normalization, no expected\n    31→      files.\n    32→  - id: F3\n    33→    step: |\n    34→      The RunDiffTests matching-output test creates two mock binaries that produce identical\n    35→      stdout and stderr, then calls RunDiffTests. The test passes silently with no output.\n    36→  - id: F4\n    37→    step: |\n    38→      The RunDiffTests divergent-output test creates two mock binaries that produce different\n    39→      stdout. RunDiffTests calls t.Fatal with a failure message containing the args, stdin,\n    40→      both stdouts, both stderrs, and both exit codes.\n    41→  - id: F5\n    42→    step: |\n    43→      The normalization test creates mock binaries whose outputs differ only in a timestamp\n    44→      field. TimestampNormalizer strips the timestamp before comparison, making the test pass.\n    45→  - id: F6\n    46→    step: |\n    47→      The ComposeNormalizers test chains two normalizer functions and verifies they are\n    48→      applied in order to both stdout and stderr before comparison.\n    49→  - id: F7\n    50→    step: |\n    51→      The file-state comparison test uses mock binaries that write to files in the working\n    52→      directory. DiffTest.ExpectedFiles specifies the expected content. The test verifies\n    53→      that matching content passes and divergent content fails with the correct report.\n    54→  - id: F8\n    55→    step: |\n    56→      The timeout test creates a mock binary that sleeps beyond the configured timeout.\n    57→      RunDiffTests fails with a clear timeout message rather than hanging.\n    58→  - id: F9\n    59→    step: |\n    60→      The environment default test verifies that LC_ALL=C is set when DiffTest.Env is nil,\n    61→      and that an explicit Env entry overrides the default.\n    62→\n    63→touchpoints:\n    64→  - T1: \"pkg/testutils — DiffTest, NormalizeFunc (prd001-testutils R1)\"\n    65→  - T2: \"pkg/testutils — RunDiffTests, WorkDir, LC_ALL default (prd001-testutils R2)\"\n    66→  - T3: \"pkg/testutils — comparison and divergence reporting (prd001-testutils R3)\"\n    67→  - T4: \"pkg/testutils — TimestampNormalizer, ComposeNormalizers (prd001-testutils R4)\"\n    68→  - T5: \"pkg/testutils — ExpectedFiles file-state comparison (prd001-testutils R5)\"\n    69→\n    70→success_criteria:\n    71→  - id: S1\n    72→    criterion: DiffTest zero value is a valid test case that runs without error.\n    73→  - id: S2\n    74→    criterion: RunDiffTests produces no output when both binaries match.\n    75→  - id: S3\n    76→    criterion: RunDiffTests reports divergence with args, stdin, both outputs, and both exit codes.\n    77→  - id: S4\n    78→    criterion: TimestampNormalizer strips strftime timestamps so that time-dependent outputs match.\n    79→  - id: S5\n    80→    criterion: ComposeNormalizers applies functions in order and the composed result works as a single normalizer.\n    81→  - id: S6\n    82→    criterion: ExpectedFiles comparison passes for matching files and fails for divergent files.\n    83→  - id: S7\n    84→    criterion: Timeout produces a clear failure message rather than hanging.\n    85→  - id: S8\n    86→    criterion: LC_ALL=C is the default environment and DiffTest.Env overrides it.\n    87→  - id: S9\n    88→    criterion: go test ./pkg/testutils/... passes with no failures.\n    89→\n    90→out_of_scope:\n    91→  - Utility-specific normalizers (LsNormalizer, LsExtendedNormalizer) are defined in their\n    92→    respective cmd/ packages, not in pkg/testutils.\n    93→  - Binary compilation and installation are handled by magefiles, not pkg/testutils.\n    94→  - Retry logic and filesystem mocking are explicitly excluded by the PRD.\n    95→\n    96→test_suite: test-rel00.0\n    97→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eeb80a62-f416-48e8-abb0-3af90791f644","uuid":"02229760-26cb-4336-b4b9-17492810d1fb","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/78/docs/specs/use-cases/rel00.0-uc004-testutils.yaml","content":"id: rel00.0-uc004-testutils\ntitle: \"Execute differential tests and compare binary outputs via pkg/testutils\"\n\nsummary: |\n  The operator verifies that pkg/testutils correctly executes Go and reference binaries\n  with identical inputs, compares their outputs, and reports divergence. The test exercises\n  each harness capability in isolation: RunDiffTests runs named subtests and compares\n  stdout, stderr, and exit code byte-for-byte; normalization hooks strip non-deterministic\n  fields before comparison; ComposeNormalizers chains multiple hooks; file-state comparison\n  validates output files for utilities like sponge; and the timeout mechanism prevents\n  hanging test runs.\n\nactor: Human Operator\n\ntrigger: |\n  The operator has completed the PRD revision (prd001-testutils.yaml) and wants to verify\n  that pkg/testutils satisfies its requirements via unit tests.\n\nflow:\n  - id: F1\n    step: |\n      The operator runs go test ./pkg/testutils/... which executes the unit tests for\n      pkg/testutils. Unlike cmd/ packages that use differential testing against a reference\n      binary, pkg/testutils is the harness itself. Its tests use mock binaries (small shell\n      scripts or compiled test helpers) that produce known stdout, stderr, and exit codes.\n  - id: F2\n    step: |\n      The DiffTest struct test verifies that all fields are accessible and that the zero\n      value produces a valid test case: no args, nil stdin (EOF), nil env (defaults with\n      LC_ALL=C), empty WorkDir (t.TempDir), exit code 0, no normalization, no expected\n      files.\n  - id: F3\n    step: |\n      The RunDiffTests matching-output test creates two mock binaries that produce identical\n      stdout and stderr, then calls RunDiffTests. The test passes silently with no output.\n  - id: F4\n    step: |\n      The RunDiffTests divergent-output test creates two mock binaries that produce different\n      stdout. RunDiffTests calls t.Fatal with a failure message containing the args, stdin,\n      both stdouts, both stderrs, and both exit codes.\n  - id: F5\n    step: |\n      The normalization test creates mock binaries whose outputs differ only in a timestamp\n      field. TimestampNormalizer strips the timestamp before comparison, making the test pass.\n  - id: F6\n    step: |\n      The ComposeNormalizers test chains two normalizer functions and verifies they are\n      applied in order to both stdout and stderr before comparison.\n  - id: F7\n    step: |\n      The file-state comparison test uses mock binaries that write to files in the working\n      directory. DiffTest.ExpectedFiles specifies the expected content. The test verifies\n      that matching content passes and divergent content fails with the correct report.\n  - id: F8\n    step: |\n      The timeout test creates a mock binary that sleeps beyond the configured timeout.\n      RunDiffTests fails with a clear timeout message rather than hanging.\n  - id: F9\n    step: |\n      The environment default test verifies that LC_ALL=C is set when DiffTest.Env is nil,\n      and that an explicit Env entry overrides the default.\n\ntouchpoints:\n  - T1: \"pkg/testutils — DiffTest, NormalizeFunc (prd001-testutils R1)\"\n  - T2: \"pkg/testutils — RunDiffTests, WorkDir, LC_ALL default (prd001-testutils R2)\"\n  - T3: \"pkg/testutils — comparison and divergence reporting (prd001-testutils R3)\"\n  - T4: \"pkg/testutils — TimestampNormalizer, ComposeNormalizers (prd001-testutils R4)\"\n  - T5: \"pkg/testutils — ExpectedFiles file-state comparison (prd001-testutils R5)\"\n\nsuccess_criteria:\n  - id: S1\n    criterion: DiffTest zero value is a valid test case that runs without error.\n  - id: S2\n    criterion: RunDiffTests produces no output when both binaries match.\n  - id: S3\n    criterion: RunDiffTests reports divergence with args, stdin, both outputs, and both exit codes.\n  - id: S4\n    criterion: TimestampNormalizer strips strftime timestamps so that time-dependent outputs match.\n  - id: S5\n    criterion: ComposeNormalizers applies functions in order and the composed result works as a single normalizer.\n  - id: S6\n    criterion: ExpectedFiles comparison passes for matching files and fails for divergent files.\n  - id: S7\n    criterion: Timeout produces a clear failure message rather than hanging.\n  - id: S8\n    criterion: LC_ALL=C is the default environment and DiffTest.Env overrides it.\n  - id: S9\n    criterion: go test ./pkg/testutils/... passes with no failures.\n\nout_of_scope:\n  - Utility-specific normalizers (LsNormalizer, LsExtendedNormalizer) are defined in their\n    respective cmd/ packages, not in pkg/testutils.\n  - Binary compilation and installation are handled by magefiles, not pkg/testutils.\n  - Retry logic and filesystem mocking are explicitly excluded by the PRD.\n\ntest_suite: test-rel00.0\n","numLines":97,"startLine":1,"totalLines":97}}}
