rgs, stdin, both stdouts, both stderrs, and both exit codes\"\n    traces:\n      - prd001-testutils R3.2\n      - prd001-testutils R3.5\n\n  - name: rundifftests_divergent_exit_code\n    description: RunDiffTests reports failure when exit codes differ.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\"\n      setup: \"Go binary exits 0, reference exits 1\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: test fails with message showing both exit codes\n    traces:\n      - prd001-testutils R3.4\n      - prd001-testutils R3.5\n\n  - name: timestamp_normalizer\n    description: TimestampNormalizer strips strftime timestamps so time-dependent outputs match.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests with Normalize: []NormalizeFunc{TimestampNormalizer}\"\n      setup: \"binaries produce outputs differing only in timestamp field\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: test passes after normalization strips timestamps\n    traces:\n      - prd001-testutils R4.1\n      - prd001-testutils R4.2\n\n  - name: compose_normalizers\n    description: ComposeNormalizers chains multiple functions applied in order.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"testutils.ComposeNormalizers(fn1, fn2)\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: \"composed function applies fn1 then fn2; output matches fn2(fn1(input))\"\n    traces:\n      - prd001-testutils R4.3\n      - prd001-testutils R4.4\n\n  - name: expected_files_match\n    description: ExpectedFiles comparison passes when Go binary writes correct file content.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests with ExpectedFiles\"\n      setup: \"mock binary writes expected content to output file\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: test passes with no output\n    traces:\n      - prd001-testutils R5.1\n      - prd001-testutils R5.2\n\n  - name: expected_files_diverge\n    description: ExpectedFiles comparison fails when Go binary writes wrong file content.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests 